<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="section-4" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Webwork</title>
  <p>
    In this section, we will include samples of Webwork problems.
  </p>

<exercise label="FirstWebWork"><webwork>
  <pg-code>
    Context("LimitedNumeric");
   $a=random(2,8,1);
$b=random(2,8,1);
$c=random(2,8,1);
$ysign=list_random(0,1);
$zsign=list_random(0,1);
$sum=$ysign+$zsign+1;
if ($ysign==0) {$ysign='-'};
if ($ysign==1) {$ysign='+'};
if ($zsign==0) {$zsign='-'};
if ($zsign==1) {$zsign='+'};
if($sum==1) {$ans='a hyperboloid of two sheets'};
if($sum==2) {$ans='a hyperboloid of one sheet'};
if($sum==3) {$ans='an ellipsoid'};
  </pg-code>

<statement>
<p>
State whether the equation 

<m> \left( \frac{x}{<var name="$a"/>} \right)^2 <var name="$ysign"/> \left( \frac{y}{<var name="$b"/>} \right)^2 <var name="$zsign"/> \left( \frac{z}{<var name="$c"/>} \right)^2=1 </m>
defines:
</p>




<p>
  <ol marker="(1)">
    <li> A hyperboloid of two sheets</li>
    <li> A hyperboloid of one sheet</li>
    <li> An ellipsoid</li>
    <li> None of these</li>
  </ol>
</p>
<p>Enter number of statement that is correct: <var name="$sum" width="5"/></p> 
</statement>

  <solution>
    <p>
     This equation is the equation of <var name="$ans"/>.
    </p>
  </solution>
</webwork >
</exercise>

<figure>
      <caption> The rectangle inscribed in the ellipse. </caption>
      <image source="Rec_insc_ellipse.png" width="70%">
        <description>
          <p>The area of the rectangle is <m>f(x,y)=4xy</m> and the constraint is <m>g(x,y)=[$constraint]-[$c]=0</m>.
          </p>
        </description>
      </image>
    </figure>

<exercise label="SecondWebWork"><webwork>
  <pg-code>
    Context("Numeric");
$a = random(1,4);
$b = random(5,10);
$c = random(1,10);
Context()->variables->are(x=>"Real",y=>"Real");
$constraint = Formula("$a*x^2+$b*y^2")->reduce();
$LM1 = Compute(2*$a);
$LM2 = Compute(2*$b);
$ans = Compute("(2*$c)/(($a*$b)^(1/2))")->reduce();
  </pg-code>

<statement>
<p>
Find the maximum area of a rectangle which is inscribed in <m>[$constraint]=[$c]</m>.
</p>

</statement>

  <solution>
    <p>
The area of the rectangle is <m>f(x,y)=4xy</m> and the constraint is <m>g(x,y)=[$constraint]-[$c]=0</m>. 
Due to the Lagrange Multiplier method, we have <m>\vec{\nabla f}=\lambda \vec{\nabla g}</m>, which gives 
the following vector equation: 
    <md>\langle 4y, 4x\rangle=\lambda \langle [$LM1] x, [$LM2] y\rangle</md>.
    </p>
    <p>
This vector equation is equivalent to these two scalar equations: 
    <md>4y=[$LM1]\lambda x</md>,
    <md>4x=[$LM2]\lambda y</md>.
    </p>
    <p>
We divide the above equations: 
<md>\frac{4y}{4x}=\frac{[$LM1] \lambda x}{[$LM2] \lambda y} 
\Rightarrow \frac{y}{x}=\frac{[$LM1] x}{[$LM2] y} \Rightarrow y^2=\frac{[$a]}{[$b]} x^2</md>. 
</p>
<p>
Then, we replace this equation into 
<m>g(x,y)=[$constraint]-[$c]=0</m> to get <m>[$a]x^2+[$a]x^2=[$c]</m>. Hence, <m>x=\sqrt{\frac{[$c]}{[$LM1]}}</m> 
and <m>y=\sqrt{\frac{[$c]}{[$LM2]}}</m> and the maximum area is 
<m>4\left(\sqrt{\frac{[$c]}{[$LM1]}}\right)\left(\sqrt{\frac{[$c]}{[$LM2]}}\right)=[$ans]</m>.
    </p>
  </solution>
</webwork>
</exercise>

</section>